The plan in .agents/plans/M5O.md is approved, with one addition: the phone has to record the engine sound. Add an
Android recorder for the `engine_sound_screen` test: a record button on that test's card that captures 5-8 s of
16-bit mono PCM WAV at 44.1 kHz (AudioRecord; the squeal band reaches 6 kHz, so no low sample rates), uploads it as a
blob with the current OBD rpm and the vehicle's cylinder count, and submits it through the normal test result path.
It needs RECORD_AUDIO, requested at runtime only when the user taps record, with a plain explanation; the safety-gate
checklist (engine running, outdoors) still comes first.

A Wonder review of M5/M5U is running in parallel and only writes .agents/reviews/M5-M5U.md; don't wait for it or
touch that file. Implement the plan in its order, each step with its test before the next. Keep all existing tests
green. Run the plan's verification commands except the owner spike (backend via .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q;
Android offline with GRADLE_USER_HOME seeded from ~/.gradle), fix failures until they pass, add a dated
docs/DECISIONS.md entry, and do not commit. Finish with files created/changed, test counts and pass/fail.
